{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.729646Z","id":"814dc09f9b5d925021865fffd75b9af35d4ee37bc7a89702fde72d8949f04295","body":{"detail":"Since 827ff96 the daemon wakes a parked inject poll when wait_for_feedback starts and answers it empty. The loop then either polls again at once (it had parked over INJECT_EARLY_MS, and that poll is answered empty too, so the loop pauses) or pauses at once (parked under 1 s). Either way it can sit in an INJECT_RETRY_MS (5 s) pause after the wait ends, delaying feedback sent then.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1338},"end":{"line":1356},"content_hash":"9d3c66e7944b4fed8c1021abed8b22c9a886d0e44cfa3fc482ff9a7b0881929f"},"suggested_fix":"Make no poll and no pause while the extension's own wait_for_feedback runs, poll at once when the last wait ends, and end a retry pause when a wait starts or ends.","summary":"The Pi injection loop's pause after wait_for_feedback depends on timing","tags":["fix-pending:followups-streams-perf-pi","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:37:53.424566Z","id":"504305470894114525162f118c2de55e6d365aaaf55f595801e5adb6913ca629","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:81d184b","summary":"The extension now counts its own wait_for_feedback calls: while one runs the injection loop makes no poll and no pause, and once the last ends it polls at once; a poll answered after a wait started or ended meanwhile takes no retry pause, and an aborted wait ends its request at once (c8cdf53). plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts 'tier 5 holds while wait_for_feedback runs and polls again as soon as it ends (parked 0 ms)' and '(parked 2000 ms)', with fake timers never advanced, pass; they fail on the code before 81d184b. Pi suite: 64 passed.","supersedes":"814dc09f9b5d925021865fffd75b9af35d4ee37bc7a89702fde72d8949f04295","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.971019Z","id":"4c687df59d12a20b5ef6c0dbae9e1af56826fd4c9a2529bfbbdf152ba2edcfc3","body":{"detail":"Spec §11 has the agent side send repo and branch on registration. The Rust shim does (clax_mcp::shim::registration via clax_core::names::repo_and_branch); the Pi extension's Registration body has neither field.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":47},"end":{"line":54},"content_hash":"cd8bc6fa23d0859826c16587835194e0329e27cfa81699a90acd2a72e2ad5308"},"suggested_fix":"Read the repository and branch from the files under cwd in plugins/pi/src/client.ts (no git process) and send them.","summary":"Pi registers without repo and branch, so a Pi agent is named after its harness ('pi', 'pi-2', …)","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T08:52:10.621010Z","id":"30ef13bd774b557a1ff03179e1f5538575641fc61325026d493b8b893b52fd06","body":{"detail":"Spec §11 has the agent side send repo and branch on registration. The Rust shim does (clax_mcp::shim::registration via clax_core::names::repo_and_branch); the Pi extension's Registration body has neither field.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":47},"end":{"line":54},"content_hash":"cf70a4310d8df663e355de8659dce21e4e67136a74f40eeeda5444d4eab3d516"},"suggested_fix":"Read the repository and branch from the files under cwd in plugins/pi/src/client.ts (no git process) and send them.","summary":"Pi registers without repo and branch, so a Pi agent is named after its harness ('pi', 'pi-2', …)","supersedes":"4c687df59d12a20b5ef6c0dbae9e1af56826fd4c9a2529bfbbdf152ba2edcfc3","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T22:14:39.268743Z","id":"3cba80f8c380074b38c23937a062e8dc79a20fcca0a7292616ff4d3fe3e31589","body":{"detail":"A version lists no file withheld from the reader (files_withheld counts them), so clax_read of such a path throws not_found \"version N of X has no file '<path>'\". The Rust tools (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs do_read) instead fetch the bytes when files_withheld > 0 and hand the daemon's 403 withheld answer, which names the authors and never the path (api_mcp::the_read_tool_answers_a_withheld_file_as_withheld). no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi counts the echo as a leak of MIACANARYfilename.html.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":902},"end":{"line":903},"content_hash":"c3e5c7fe256c6b72857954f8c3afeb1c01188a8525431c01f11f9d0c25906cd5"},"summary":"Pi's read tool reports a withheld file as missing and echoes the name it was asked for","tags":["visibility","depends:task-19","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T00:51:56.798244Z","id":"23ac73e97d3388ba1ca3a035834f70459741765df9271876e0d3aa36cc681de7","body":{"detail":"docView keeps id, path, data, version and updated_at, so the daemon's placeholder {doc_id, version, withheld: {authors}} becomes {version} with exists: true, and dbList (plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1173) never passes withheld_count on. Nothing leaks, but a Pi agent reads Mia's document as empty and its listing as complete, where the Rust tools (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs doc_view and do_db_list) and clax db say it is withheld and by whom.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":440},"end":{"line":442},"content_hash":"7628b2d8f4308706fedbc0ff68e336d720b50d5273ef1ce11046b7d868512b4c"},"suggested_fix":"Mirror crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs doc_view: a document with withheld becomes {id: doc_id, version, withheld}; copy withheld_count into the listing when present; add a Pi test with a placeholder.","summary":"Pi's db tools show a withheld document as an existing document with only a version, and drop a listing's withheld_count","tags":["people","depends:task-19","review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:09.794902Z","id":"e6f38a6ad1d1b56edf01c256dbd6438091db680a0a52f9ebc0fc84f49d2a0a39","body":{"detail":"handoverOf keeps feedback, answers and text; a poll that hands over only placeholders (spec §8.3: N comments from <name> ... are withheld) has empty feedback, so Pi's piggyback and wait_for_feedback treat it as nothing handed over and drop the text, and wait_for_feedback says call_again. The injection loop sends res.text and so carries them. The MCP shim's Handover (crates/clax-mcp/src/render.rs) counts withheld. Pi's sweep (api_canary::no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi) also still reports one leak: an error echoing a path the call named, 'version 1 of <id> has no file MIACANARYfilename.html'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":272},"end":{"line":272},"content_hash":"f537bc15e77c9dfe41600cf783ff302b8ddbd572a675a9437d7b88482c530940"},"summary":"Pi's tool-result handover ignores the feedback poll's withheld placeholders","tags":["people","depends:task-19","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.887595Z","id":"602b52bc0e7c50a092999bdee0cd1c9be8f7cbe70ec8d673d05457d4c73a3241","body":{"detail":"A version lists no file withheld from the reader (files_withheld counts them), so clax_read of such a path throws not_found \"version N of X has no file '<path>'\". The Rust tools (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs do_read) instead fetch the bytes when files_withheld > 0 and hand the daemon's 403 withheld answer, which names the authors and never the path (api_mcp::the_read_tool_answers_a_withheld_file_as_withheld). no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi counts the echo as a leak of MIACANARYfilename.html.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":909},"end":{"line":910},"content_hash":"c3e5c7fe256c6b72857954f8c3afeb1c01188a8525431c01f11f9d0c25906cd5"},"summary":"Pi's read tool reports a withheld file as missing and echoes the name it was asked for","supersedes":"3cba80f8c380074b38c23937a062e8dc79a20fcca0a7292616ff4d3fe3e31589","tags":["visibility","depends:task-19","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.888162Z","id":"a37fe1ccd67c67e5ba49647f223686d24807edafd952e711ac7964eaf4f9fae8","body":{"detail":"docView keeps id, path, data, version and updated_at, so the daemon's placeholder {doc_id, version, withheld: {authors}} becomes {version} with exists: true, and dbList (plugins/pi/src/clax.ts:1173) never passes withheld_count on. Nothing leaks, but a Pi agent reads Mia's document as empty and its listing as complete, where the Rust tools (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs doc_view and do_db_list) and clax db say it is withheld and by whom.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":447},"end":{"line":449},"content_hash":"7628b2d8f4308706fedbc0ff68e336d720b50d5273ef1ce11046b7d868512b4c"},"suggested_fix":"Mirror crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs doc_view: a document with withheld becomes {id: doc_id, version, withheld}; copy withheld_count into the listing when present; add a Pi test with a placeholder.","summary":"Pi's db tools show a withheld document as an existing document with only a version, and drop a listing's withheld_count","supersedes":"23ac73e97d3388ba1ca3a035834f70459741765df9271876e0d3aa36cc681de7","tags":["people","depends:task-19","review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:48.888737Z","id":"6ec316978fc87509b44ef951dd8d4c8613116be6adcd7e30f21ee2c0e30d6821","body":{"detail":"handoverOf keeps feedback, answers and text; a poll that hands over only placeholders (spec §8.3: N comments from <name> ... are withheld) has empty feedback, so Pi's piggyback and wait_for_feedback treat it as nothing handed over and drop the text, and wait_for_feedback says call_again. The injection loop sends res.text and so carries them. The MCP shim's Handover (crates/clax-mcp/src/render.rs) counts withheld. Pi's sweep (api_canary::no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi) also still reports one leak: an error echoing a path the call named, 'version 1 of <id> has no file MIACANARYfilename.html'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":275},"end":{"line":275},"content_hash":"f537bc15e77c9dfe41600cf783ff302b8ddbd572a675a9437d7b88482c530940"},"summary":"Pi's tool-result handover ignores the feedback poll's withheld placeholders","supersedes":"e6f38a6ad1d1b56edf01c256dbd6438091db680a0a52f9ebc0fc84f49d2a0a39","tags":["people","depends:task-19","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:12:47.262999Z","id":"1420a49a5d91a92e7e1aa8100d7ae5dc8272618f0706e9dae45464f3a196557e","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 §6.8: a grant request naming a session without X-Clax-Session-Secret is 401 invalid_session_proof. Pi has no remote mode at this point (plan Task 19 adds it), and local Pi uses the daemon token, which needs no secret. Task 19's remote client must take session_secret from its registration answer, send it on every request naming the session, write <home>/remote-sessions/pi-<harness session ID>.json (0600) as the shim does (clax_core::remote::SessionFiles), treat invalid_session_proof like unknown_session (register again), and remove the file at session end.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":321},"end":{"line":325},"content_hash":"c5e149f6190b9213f5362845bd146d5472da763dff33d4e84efcd2d3356b2f9a"},"summary":"Pi's remote mode must send its session's secret beside X-Clax-Session and keep it on disk for its clax children","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.736131Z","id":"1a0c9802ee5ef3d4779cf14569819e3f3d3784c5a6c65f22a9dc897f8bf4af86","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"Pi's remote mode signs every request (plugins/pi/src/remote.ts), takes session_secret from registration, sends X-Clax-Session-Secret beside X-Clax-Session, writes remote-sessions/pi-s-<id>.json 0600 (dir 0700), registers again on invalid_session_proof or unknown_session, and removes the file at session end. Evidence: plugins/pi/test/remote.test.ts 'signs every request, proves its session with its secret, keeps it in its credential file, and registers again when the proof is refused' passes; api_canary::no_canary_reaches_a_persons_agent_through_pi_in_remote_mode drives the real Pi as Sam's agent and passes.","supersedes":"1420a49a5d91a92e7e1aa8100d7ae5dc8272618f0706e9dae45464f3a196557e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.739729Z","id":"e57123c13178c291a3897dbec4469a0ebee5b73bbfe1ddc1c92024db9bed9fc1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"Pi's read fetches the bytes when files_withheld > 0 and hands the daemon's 403 withheld answer, as crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs do_read does. Evidence: api_canary::no_canary_reaches_an_agent_through_pi (real Pi in RPC mode) passes; with the fetch removed it reports 'leaked MIACANARYfilename.html' and 'MIACANARYcarried.css'.","supersedes":"602b52bc0e7c50a092999bdee0cd1c9be8f7cbe70ec8d673d05457d4c73a3241","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.740568Z","id":"3f7eda6619dce9beb7a2229e05bffb8bb2df0b9876fab08f80b9fb2756df7ae9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"handoverOf keeps withheld; handedOver counts it; results carry withheld and notes as the Rust render does; wait_for_feedback's call_again is false when placeholders arrive. Evidence: plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts 'withheld placeholders alone count as handed over' passes; the read echo is closed with 602b52bc.","supersedes":"6ec316978fc87509b44ef951dd8d4c8613116be6adcd7e30f21ee2c0e30d6821","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/clax.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.741416Z","id":"b8329d7f99736c5a543ec0d5222c51f8d6777bfae41e9465056407ed71d60363","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"docView mirrors doc_view (a withheld document is {id: doc_id, version, withheld}) and db_list passes withheld_count on. Evidence: plugins/pi/test/remote.test.ts 'the db tools show a withheld document as withheld ...' passes, and api_canary::no_canary_reaches_a_persons_agent_through_pi_in_remote_mode sees withheld_count 2 for Mia's documents.","supersedes":"a37fe1ccd67c67e5ba49647f223686d24807edafd952e711ac7964eaf4f9fae8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.742259Z","id":"a13bdc6cbab35a978d06cc0646e6102639ea182d9d4e70733b19a84600610f2a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"Pi's registration carries repo and branch from repoAndBranch (plugins/pi/src/git.ts, no git process, as clax_core::names::repo_and_branch). Evidence: plugins/pi/test/clax.test.ts 'registers with the repository and branch of its working directory, which name the agent' (name chart-repo-axis) and remote.test.ts 'reads the repository and branch from the files' pass.","supersedes":"30ef13bd774b557a1ff03179e1f5538575641fc61325026d493b8b893b52fd06","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/remote.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.744932Z","id":"e188ad6f43d6776280e7641753961434c137ab316ab3f45c2c8c3b22abbc1a04","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 §6.8 opens every credential file through the directory's own handle (openat with O_NOFOLLOW), as clax_core::remote::SessionFiles does. Node has no openat, so SessionFiles here lstats <home>/remote-sessions and then opens <dir>/<name> with O_NOFOLLOW on the last component only. Another process of the same OS user could race a symlink in for the directory; that user can already read the machine's key (§6.8's trust limit), so this stops no attacker the Rust client stops, but it is weaker than the spec's wording.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":214},"end":{"line":298},"content_hash":"a758379c62d93f046a2f1ca484e5bb5a7e1d760a2a3335042e964175402e0b5b"},"suggested_fix":"Open the directory with fs.opendirSync and compare its dev/ino before and after each file open, or keep the file I/O in a `clax` subcommand.","summary":"Pi's credential files check the directory with lstat, then open the file by path with O_NOFOLLOW: a directory swapped for a symbolic link between the two is followed","tags":["security","remote","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"plugins/pi/src/client.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.745014Z","id":"41fdb3011b477eeb4e9bc44a85f0e8c5df84e148c0d565512a1e9ebfdc59674a","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08 §6.8 names a row with a parent PID also <harness>-p-<parent PID>.json, written only when the parent's start time can be told. The extension cannot read a process's start time without a child process, so it writes no such file; a client that knows Pi's process but not its session ID finds no credential. No client does so today (Codex's shim is the only parent-PID reader).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":323},"end":{"line":326},"content_hash":"413c6068cf75a3a7ecab204dc282c96261df3978b01faee6d7443dcd828961af"},"summary":"Pi writes its session's credential under its harness session ID only, never a parent-PID file","tags":["remote","revisit:a client looks up Pi's credential by parent PID","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
